<AtTheTable>
  Before adding two lists of cards that might help you, check whether any
  physical card appears in both lists. Count each helpful outcome once. The
  later outs chapter will apply this directly to overlapping draws; this lesson
  supplies the bookkeeping before adding the extra question of whether an
  apparent improvement really wins.
</AtTheTable>

<QuantCorner>
  Two risk descriptions can refer to the same underlying scenario. Adding their
  probabilities without checking overlap can overstate the chance that at least
  one risk occurs. Inclusion–exclusion is the basic accounting step before
  building a more detailed dependence model.
</QuantCorner>
